==Esperanto==

===Etymology===
Latin, Italian ''[[venire]]'' and French ''[[venir]]''

===Verb===
{{eo-verb|ven}}

# to [[come]]
#: Mi venus al via partio, sed mi malsanigis la gripon.
#: ''I would come to your party, but I contracted influenza.''

====Conjugation====
{{eo-conj|ven|intr=yes}}

===See also===
* {{l|eo|alveni|gloss=to [[arrive]]}}
* {{l|eo|deveni|gloss=to [[originate]], to come from}}
* {{l|eo|elveni|gloss=to come out, to exit}}
* {{l|eo|enveni|gloss=to come into, to enter}}
* {{l|eo|kunveni|gloss=to [[gather]], to [[congregate]]}}
* {{l|eo|reveni|gloss=to [[return]]; to come back}}

{{eo BRO|2}}

